"""
HoloRAID v3.0 (HyperMorphic Gearbox) — Intricate Image Reconstruction Benchmark
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

What this does:
- Generates a highly intricate 16-bit grayscale image (fractal + interference + rings).
- Encodes every pixel as a secret s ∈ [0, Q] using CORRECT Asmuth–Bloom (shadow prime p0 > Q).
- Splits into n shards, then simulates shard loss (up to n-k erasures).
- Decodes from any k shards and verifies BIT-PERFECT reconstruction.

Colab:
- Paste this whole file into a single cell and run.
- No installs needed (NumPy + Matplotlib are preinstalled on Colab).

Notes on correctness:
- Uses a sequential (Garner-style) CRT lift that stays within int64 range for k=3,
  avoiding uint64 overflow that breaks "vectorized CRT sum-of-products" methods.

Authors: Shaun Gerrard + Claude (HyperMorphic Mathematics Research)
Date: 2026-01-03
"""

import math
